    "recent_exchanges": [
      {
        "user": "I'm checking Medicare coverage for myself in Collier County. I'd like to keep my cardiologist and understand what visits could cost. Where should I start?",
        "assistant": "Start with two things: the coverage route and your doctor/cost checks. Medicare has two main paths: Original Medicare is Parts A and B through the federal program; Medicare Advantage is a private plan that provides Parts A and B. With Original Medicare, you can add a separate drug plan and may be able to buy Medigap to help with your share of costs. With Advantage, most plans include drug coverage. You still pay the Part B premium either way. For visit costs, don’t look only at the monthly premium—total cost also includes deductibles, copays, and coinsurance when you use care. Since keeping your cardiologist matters, the next comparison is whether the exact doctor and office participate in the exact plan, because that isn’t established yet.",
        "question": "What ZIP code do you live in? That helps narrow the local Medicare options in the county before we compare doctor access and likely visit costs."
      },
      {
        "user": "I currently have Aetna Medicare Advantage. My cardiologist is Dr. Maya Reed at Cypress Heart Clinic in Naples. I don't know the exact plan name.",
        "assistant": "That gives us a useful start. We know you’re on a Medicare Advantage plan, and you’ve named the cardiologist and office you want to keep. What we still do **not** know is the exact Aetna plan, so we can’t tell yet whether Dr. Maya Reed at Cypress Heart Clinic in Naples participates in **your specific plan** or what a cardiology visit would cost under it. A carrier name alone isn’t enough for that check. For visit costs, the pieces to compare are the monthly premium and what you pay when you use care, like deductibles, copays, or coinsurance.",
        "question": "What ZIP code do you live in? That helps narrow the Medicare plans available in your area while we sort out doctor access and visit costs."
      }
    ],
    "current_message": "Before we go further, what does Medicare Advantage mean? Does the office accepting Aetna prove it takes my particular plan?",
